# Plex API Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
#
# The suite reads only testing/e2e/.env. It never reads the repository root
# .env, which holds the OUTTAKE_* application configuration rather than the
# PLEX_* credentials these specs need.
#
# A variable already exported in the shell always wins over the file, so
#
#     PLEX_TOKEN=... task test-e2e
#
# overrides whatever this file carries. `export KEY=value` lines, quoted values,
# comments, and blank lines are all understood. A line whose value is blank is
# treated as absent rather than as an empty credential.
#
# Both PLEX_TOKEN and PLEX_SERVER_URL must resolve for the Plex specs to run.
# When either is missing those specs skip and everything else still runs.
#
# ffmpeg and ffprobe must be on PATH for the clip and preview specs to run: the
# suite generates a one-second test pattern with ffmpeg and renders against it.
# When either binary is missing those specs skip and everything else still runs.
#
# Run the suite with `task test-e2e`.

# Your Plex authentication token
# Obtain from: https://support.plex.tv/articles/204059436-finding-an-authentication-token-x-plex-token/
PLEX_TOKEN=your_plex_token_here

# Optional: Plex server URL for E2E tests
PLEX_SERVER_URL=https://plex.example.com

# Optional: Client ID for Plex API requests
PLEX_CLIENT_ID=outtake